# A step that gives back what its call gives hands that value on through its own arrow, also where its written return is
# another shape of the same array: `branch` returns `projection(image)` as `Float[Tensor, "batch 16"]`, and `Projection.forward`
# gives `Float[Tensor, "*lead {self.out}"]`. The language reads both as `Tensor`; the shape refines that type, so what
# the call gives is of a type `branch` gives (mathematics.md, "Shapes and their rank").

route encoders.model.project
step project/batch
step project/Projection()
step project/branch
step project/branch/Projection.forward

line entry > project call
line project/batch > Float[Tensor, batch 384]·image@project/batch value
line project/Projection() > Projection@project/Projection() value
line Projection@project/Projection() > project/branch/Projection.forward value              # the projection the call runs on
line Float[Tensor, batch 384]·image@project/batch > project/branch/Projection.forward value
line project/branch/Projection.forward > Float[Tensor, *lead {self.out}]@project/branch/Projection.forward value
line Float[Tensor, *lead {self.out}]@project/branch/Projection.forward > project/branch value  # body hands back what it made
line project/branch > Float[Tensor, batch 16]·z@project/branch value
line Float[Tensor, batch 16]·z@project/branch > project value                                # print(z)
line project > Screen own

home Float[Tensor, batch 384]·image@project/batch project
home Projection@project/Projection() project
home Float[Tensor, *lead {self.out}]@project/branch/Projection.forward project/branch
home Float[Tensor, batch 16]·z@project/branch project

side entry left
side Screen right
